  "body": "**Stacked on #333** (`issue/257-gcode-comments`, which touches every `.cps` post). This diff includes #333's commits until it merges; the #173 work itself is the last commit. Review #333 first.\n\n## What changed\n- **`haas.cps`: probes.** It adds `onProbeMove` / `onProbeRetreat` / `onProbeResult`:\n  - G31 skip; #5061–#5063 trip read; no-contact and out-of-tolerance alarms through `#3000`;\n  - incremental G91 back-off;\n  - `G10 L2 P` from `#5221+20×slot`, or a `#3006` operator stop.\n  - Source: the Haas Mill Operator's Manual (public).\n- **`mazak.cps`: probes.** The same macro-B contract in Mazak EIA/ISO words:\n  - `IF[..]GOTO` with unique N labels, since `IF..THEN` is not documented on every EIA generation;\n  - the operator stop is a comment plus M00.\n  - Source: Mazak's EIA/ISO programming manual (Fanuc-compatible).\n- **`sinumerik.cps`: probes.**\n  - `MEAS=1 G1`; `$AC_MEA[1]` checks for no contact; `$AA_MW[..]` reads the trip into R50–R61.\n  - `IF..ENDIF` + `MSG` + `SETAL` + `M0` alarms; incremental G91 back-off.\n  - Sets the offset through `$P_UIFR[..,TR]` (FI copied when the frame changes), then re-selects the active G5x.\n  - It refuses by name to set G58/G59 (axial offsets on an 840D) or to work from an offset outside G54–G57 / G505–G599.\n  - Source: SINUMERIK 840D sl Programming Manual (Fundamentals / Job Planning).\n- **`heidenhain.cps`: still refused by name.** The TNC 640 ISO manual this post follows documents no skip move and no trip-position variable; TNC probing lives in the separate touch-probe-cycles manual. The script now carries a comment saying so, and the existing engine refusal is pinned.\n- **Spindle at 0 rpm.** Haas, Mazak and Siemens no longer write a spindle-on block at 0 rpm (a touch probe), as fanuc already did. No existing golden contained `S0`.\n- `docs/decisions/173-probe-hooks-dialects.md` names every source and judgement call.\n\n## How tested\n- New `crates/app/tests/probe_dialects.rs` (7 tests): bore-centre goldens `golden/nc/{haas,mazak,sinumerik}/probe_bore_centre.nc` (G55 set from G54), both operator-stop variants, the Sinumerik G59 refusal, and the Heidenhain refusal.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` (macOS): post suites ok. App suites: everything passes except `probe_op::every_older_kind_keeps_its_stored_id_and_digest_tag`. That test pins `PROJECT_VERSION == 51`, but main is now at 53, so it fails the same way on `upstream/main`; PR #345 fixes it. This commit touches no Rust source.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- **No controller or simulator run yet**, so this stays a draft. The posted words follow the public manuals only.\n  - Mazak is the weakest-sourced: its `#5061` / `#5221` numbering should be confirmed against a Mazak manual.\n  - Sinumerik's MEAS/`$AA_MW` path needs a check on a real 840D or a simulator.\n- **The probe is not armed by the post.** Arming is machine-specific and stated by no stream record. An unarmed probe never trips, so it raises the no-contact alarm, which matches fanuc.\n\nChangelog: The Haas, Mazak and Siemens 840D posts write the Probe operation (skip move, trip read, tolerance alarm, set work offset); Heidenhain keeps a named refusal (#173)\n\nFixes #173\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
